Local review patch: contain uncertain T6032 stop/reset transitions
Base: reviewed m1n1 2460b604c6f016956ead711823605eea840c602e with adapted SMP/index guards
Provenance: AI-assisted Debian project work; not submitted upstream.

A normal-stop timeout leaves the acknowledgement flag set. On T6032, enter
the non-returning panic path instead of allowing a later startup/handoff to
accept that flag. Preserve legacy stop-timeout continuation on other SoCs.
Do not clear or reuse a possibly live CPU's published reset/spin state.

Before reset-entry indexed publication, reject an out-of-range index. On
T6032, also reject an unmatched MPIDR that would overwrite a previously
registered fallback slot. A never-registered initial-entry slot remains
allowed; no ADT-to-MPIDR encoding or native entry sequence is invented here.
Deep-sleep's presumed-stop delay and physical reset/identity behavior remain
unqualified. This comparison series is not a boot-approved native candidate.

--- a/src/smp.c
